* We have a bit of room in the zero page space overlapping Rect2* and Temp2.  Use these as approrpiate, starting with Rect2* as space for frequently used flags.BufHandle      equ Rect2+14            ; see RgnDefs.EqusBufPtr         equ BufHandle+4Index          equ BufPtr+6ArcFlag        equ Rect2InnerFlag      equ ArcFlag+2SkipFlag       equ InnerFlag+2MidVert        equ SkipFlag+2* We get the pen size twice, once to see if there is anything to do* and once to get the actual values.  This saves us zero page space.PenHeight      equ Temp2PenWidth       equ Temp2+2* AngleFromSlope and SlopeFromAngle do not use Temp or Temp2 per se.  They* use them to pass and receive values as shown below.  No other routines* are called within the body of the two procedures (except each other).* Note that Slope2 is used to save the result from SlopeFromAngle.  It* is also on the first zero page as defined below.Angle          equ Temp                ; parameter/result both routinesSlopeSign      equ Temp+2              ; temp variableSlope          equ Temp2               ; parameter for AngleFromSlope* Now we start at EndOfSlabs and allocate variables which are used in* the oval loop.ArcAngle       equ EndOfSlab           ; 2StartAngle     equ ArcAngle+2          ; 4SkipTop        equ StartAngle+2        ; 6SkipBot        equ SkipTop+2           ; 8Flag1          equ SkipBot+2           ; 10Flag2          equ Flag1+2             ; 12Slope1         equ Flag2+2             ; 16Slope2         equ Slope1+4            ; also used in SlopeFromAngleLine1          equ Slope2+4            ; 24Line2          equ Line1+4             ; 28OuterLeft      equ Line2+4             ; 30OuterRight     equ OuterLeft+2         ; 32InnerLeft      equ OuterRight+2        ; 34InnerRight     equ InnerLeft+2         ; 36OldOuterLeft   equ InnerRight+2        ; 38OldOuterRight  equ OldOuterLeft+2      ; 40 - 6 bytes to spare* We can overlap our less frequently used variables on top of some used* only within the loop.  These are used only during initialization.HollowFlag     equ Line2+4StopAngle      equ HollowFlag+2MidHoriz       equ StopAngle+2* Now we apportion the variables within each oval recordOvalTop        equ 0OvalLeft       equ OvalTop+2OvalBottom     equ OvalLeft+2OvalRight      equ OvalBottom+2OvalHeight     equ OvalRight+2OvalWidth      equ OvalHeight+2ORightEdge     equ OvalWidth+2OLeftEdge      equ ORightEdge+4Rsqysq         equ OLeftEdge+4Square         equ Rsqysq+4OddNum         equ Square+8OddBump        equ OddNum+8OvalY          equ OddBump+8EndOval        equ OvalY+2* Last but not least, the oval record offsetsOuterOval      equ 512                 ; the beginning of the third zero pageInnerOval      equ OuterOval+EndOval